---
title: Chocolate-Pumpkin Cheesecake Bars
cookTime: 30 minutes
totalTime: 50 minutes
source.name: Taste of Home 2013
source.url: http://www.tasteofhome.com/recipes/Chocolate-Pumpkin-Cheesecake-Bars
tags: Desserts
---

Preheat the oven to 350°F.

In a microwave, melt @butter{1/3%cup}(cubed) and @unsweetened chocolate{1.5%oz}(coarsely chopped); stir until smooth.
Cool slightly.

In a #large bowl{}, dissolve @instant coffee granules{1%tbsp} in @water{1/2%cup}(boiling).
Stir in the @canned pumpkin{1%cup}, @eggs{2}(lightly beaten), and chocolate mixture.

Combine the @all-purpose flour{2%cups}, @sugar{1.5%cup}, @baking soda{3/4%tsp}, and @salt{1/2%tsp}; gradually add to chocolate mixture.

Transfer to a 15-in. x 10-in. x 1-in. #baking pan{} coated with @cooking spray{}.

= Cheesecake Batter =
In a small bowl, beat @cream cheese{8%oz}(reduced-fat) and @canned pumpkin{1/2%cup} until smooth.

Beat in the @sugar{1/4%cup}, @vanilla extract{1%tsp}, @ground cinnamon{3/4%tsp}, 
@ground ginger{3/4%tsp}, and @ground cloves{1/8%tsp}.

Add @egg{1}; beat on low speed just until combined. 
Spoon over chocolate batter.

Cut through batter with a knife to swirl the cheesecake portion. 
Sprinkle with @chocolate chips{1%cup}(semi-sweet).

Bake for ~{20-25%minutes} or until a toothpick inserted near the center comes out with moist crumbs (do not overbake).

Cool on a wire rack. Cut into bars. Refrigerate leftovers.
